Subject: Minor bug or inconsistancy?

When you want to buy a wand you shouldn't have to pay for the charge.
For that matter the cost of a wand should be proportional to the number
of charges it has that way the wand with only a "You wrest one more" from
it costs a base fee, and each charge cost some fix amount.

	This seem to me to be contradictory arguments.  Let us say that 
a wand of fire with 10 charges is worth 1000 zorkmids.  You want to use 
up 10 charges fighting some nasties in the shop, but then owe nothing 
because the wand has zero charges?

	I think you should be charged for each usage for a number of 
reasons.  If you didn't know what kind of wand it was, using it just 
taught you something.  I've paid enough college bills to know that 
knowledge doesn't come cheap.  Second, by using the wand once, you've 
made it less valuable to the next person that comes in.  Even if you buy 
the wand after using the charges, you did use it in his shop.  Think of 
it as a rehersal hall rental fee type of thing.

	As for wands costing something proportional to the number of 
charges, if scrolls of charging didn't exist I might agree.  But you 
could take that zero charges left wand of death and charge it up.  You 
buy the potential that the item has.  Some folks look at used cars and 
see old clunkers, others see something they could fix up and sell for 
twice as much.  The shopkeeper just looks at the used up old ratty wands 
he's got as 'fix 'er uppers'.

